    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d219">

                <pb facs="0241" n="171" sameAs="frus:frus1934v04/pg171"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/4015: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gibson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-08-16T20:00:00-03:00">August 16, 1934—8
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 9:55 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>175. 1. Brazilian Minister at La Paz advises Foreign Office Bolivian Minister for
                    Foreign Affairs annoyed at contradictory statements <pb facs="0242" n="172"
                        xml:id="pg172"/> he is receiving concerning bases of conciliation discussed
                    in Buenos Aires between the Brazilian Ambassador, American Ambassador, and
                    Saavedra Lamas.</p>
                <p>2. Bolivian Minister for Foreign Affairs wishes the arbitration to be <hi
                        rendition="#italic">de juris</hi> and not simple in character. He further
                    asserts that as far as Bolivia is concerned the concession of a port on the
                    Paraguay River must be made <hi rendition="#italic">sine qua non</hi> part of
                    the bases for the conciliation and that this item was apparently omitted in the
                    above mentioned conversations held in Buenos Aires.</p>
                <p>3. Saavedra Lamas yesterday informed Brazilian Ambassador that he is in
                    possession of Paraguayan note of last July accepting all seven bases for the
                    conciliation although apparently Paraguay now declares that it can only accept
                    the first and last mentioned bases.</p>
                <p>4. Brazilian Minister for Foreign Affairs is today telegraphing
                        Freitas-Valle<anchor n="18" xml:id="d219-f1"/> to consult with you
                    concerning the joint action which should be taken by us at Buenos Aires in view
                    of the present attitude of Paraguay and Bolivia.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>Repeated to Buenos Aires.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gibson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
